namespace BoatsNBeasts.Core;

internal static partial class DeepRoutes
{
    internal static readonly DeepWrit[][] Inner=[
        [
            new("The wrong side up","Dita paid a yard for twelve reversible oarlocks. Its receivers have sold one half of every pair to the fleet and the other half to a shipbreaker. She recognizes her own tool marks from a skiff's length away.","Identify the receiving ships and reclaim the paired oarlocks.","Raspjaw","The rowlocks work whichever way the boat is floating. Dita keeps the one on which the shipbreaker had scratched a recipe for rust."),
            new("The baker under the cells","Bram's sister hears knocking from beneath the bread oven. The prison plans end at the flour cellar. She has been sending down buns on the lowest lift and somebody has been sending the plate back clean.","Descend through the prison services and bring the people below to the public stair.","The Flour Bailiff","Three old stokers sit on the oven steps in their socks, eating buns from the top down. All three turn out to be excellent locksmiths."),
            new("Tax on a cloud","A revenue squadron has been collecting fines for the twins' smoke signals. The fine books list every occasion when the twins warned a fishing family off the rocks. The families want the books for a different reason.","Find the collectors and return the smoke books to the signal crews.","Captain Slake","Every warning becomes the name of a boat that came home. Uli reads them to Una until dark."),
            new("The room behind the shell","Fen has heard three different scratchings inside the turtle's old firing chambers. One is a hatching egg. One is the abandoned oven's draft. The third always comes just after somebody calls for help.","Open the old firing levels and find who is answering the hatchling.","The Clinker Hen","An apprentice has spent two nights talking to the egg through a flue. Fen promotes her to someone who is allowed to take a day off."),
            new("The freight of empty bowls","The clay fleet is ready to launch. The commission boat is taking its final fee in bowls from children's suppers. Sima asks for one bowl from each district back before the launch bell.","Break the collector squadron and bring the freight boats through the cool slips.","The Second Assessor","The youngest pilot has drawn a ferry in the bottom of her bowl. The older pilots order flags made to match.")
        ],[
            new("The pencil convoy","The school porter recognizes pupils' chair backs in the rails of a requisition barge. The barge is about to sell them for kindling. Every back is marked with the height of a child in a flood year.","Track the requisition fleet and recover the school timber.","Foreman Coot","The children stand the chair backs up at the landing. The old flood line is now low enough for them to help a smaller child past."),
            new("The mint below the leaves","Soss finds that the counterfeit leaves come from a mint built under the bank. One press is still working on the greenest leaves. Its operator has never been up to see what a live one looks like.","Enter the mint from the low ferry stair and open a route for its workers.","Copper Toad","Soss lets the mint apprentice pick his own first fare. He chooses a leaf with a hole in it, to see whether the ferry still goes."),
            new("The traveling dead-letter office","A sorting ship has been buying mail whenever a tide carries away the address. The coot has been following it for twenty years. It lands on Alba's shoulder when it finally recognizes a sail.","Find the sorting ship among the delta traders and give its letters a second delivery.","Skipper Nib","A letter addressed to The Tall Boy by the Landing reaches a very short old man. He has kept the same cap."),
            new("The trapdoor audience","Mallo's theater barge has a second stage below its boards. During the flood the audience sheltered beneath the scenery and discovered an entire painted town stretching past the footlights.","Lead the stranded company through the lower stages and raise the river curtain.","The Prompt Pike","At the curtain call half the company bows from underneath. The audience recognizes the missing lemonade cart by its squeak."),
            new("What the river kept","Pell needs a sheet that can hold a tune in floodwater. The old paper mill dried its finest work on racks underneath the delta. The families who worked there still sing the steps in order.","Find the drying floors and carry their surviving sheet up to the mill families.","The Rag Binder","The sheet dries with little blue islands in it. A ferryman raises it to his mouth and plays the way home.")
        ],[
            new("The half-tree tender","A timber tender has bought the half of Hennel's tree hanging over water. Its deed also buys every pear that has already fallen in. One of the pears has grown a floating root.","Lay claim to the drift fleet and tow the living graft to Hennel.","Captain Burl","Hennel gives the first floating pear to his granddaughter. She plants it in a bath with a life belt round the rim."),
            new("The kitchen under midnight","Pav's ladle rope runs down past the terrace to a row of old kitchen floors. A smell of burnt sugar is coming up from the lowest one. He remembers his mother's first job down there.","Follow the serving lifts and open the closed kitchens to the night cooks.","The Caramel Rook","There is a spoon under the stove with Pav's initials on it. He leaves a new one there for somebody else to find."),
            new("The finish boat","A race promoter has lifted the old finish rafter aboard a strongbox ship. Nim recognizes the white paint. She also recognizes the names of the slowest pilots, scraped off the public side.","Intercept the strongbox fleet and recover the whole finish board.","The Ribbon Kite","The pilots turn the board round halfway through the prize giving. Both sides get the same applause."),
            new("The unlit nursery","Sera's apprentice built a glasshouse underneath the main one. It has no windows to the sea. The youngest lamp trees have learned to lean toward a lantern carried by a person.","Lead the crew through the dark glass floors and open the nursery shutters.","The Mirror Moth","The trees turn toward the stars. The smallest one still turns when Sera walks past, and this pleases her."),
            new("The last crate of winter","Someone has bought the winter harvest twice and is shipping the second invoice as proof that the pears don't exist. Ilo has a very real bite mark in her sleeve from the last crate.","Catch the paper harvest and deliver the fruit to the pilots' winter boats.","Captain Pith","Each lamp in the north burns inside the outline of a pear. A moth sails to the ice on the smell of breakfast.")
        ],[
            new("A hot meal in ballast","A licensed supply fleet is piling hot stones into its ballast while the upstairs flats freeze. Tavi knows which stones belong to which kitchen because of the marks from the pots.","Take the heat boats and bring their stones back to the flats.","The Coal Diver","The kitchens light up in order from the ground floor. The last stone keeps an old cat warm on the step."),
            new("The fifth bath plug","Osa discovers that every tune in the village has been missing one note. Its pipe descends through the old public baths to the ice below the pan.","Find the stopped pipe beneath the baths and bring the lowest note back to the houses.","Boiler Piper","The missing note sounds like a person letting go of a long breath. The band agrees to play it only when it has earned the rest."),
            new("A road the books could float","The survey fleet has removed the road signs because the floe moved. Meri sends the children to identify the sign ship by the chalk marks on its mast. They find four ships with the same marks.","Board the survey flotilla and recover each classroom's moving road signs.","The Datum Goose","The children hang the signs from the handrails instead. The arrows stay correct for as long as somebody is holding them."),
            new("Ferry underneath the mountain","Ren's wife's old whistle came from a signal pipe inside the shelf. The night boats used to pass through these chambers before anyone could afford an open-water lamp.","Explore the warm passages under the ice and open the old ferry station.","The Geyser Loon","The night fare is paid in songs again. Ren sends the first song down the pipe and waits for the echo."),
            new("Four nights of warm water","The infirmary keeps its longest pipes under the tide. An old valve has shut the branch to the cottages. Anet carries a wrench big enough to need its own porter.","Descend the valve chambers and reopen the winter water circuit.","The Service Ox","A kettle begins to steam in a week-empty house. Neighbors come in out of the cold and make use of it.")
        ],[
            new("The boat with a missing button","A fastener buyer has bought the yellow coat by weight from a salvage fleet. Sib thinks the receipt is fair but insists whoever wears the coat ought to be allowed to finish doing it up.","Find the boat carrying the yellow coat among the cloth prizes.","The Buttonhook","Its new owner fits the last button to the wrong hole. Sib fixes it with one small, immensely satisfied tug."),
            new("The first stretcher stair","Hal remembers every corner on the underground stretcher road by the distance between his elbows. He could find it in his sleep. The mills have filled the road with winding machinery.","Make a way through the mill service levels wide enough for an occupied stretcher.","The Bobbin Bearer","Hal rides the first stretcher through so his old patients can carry him for once. They take corners with extraordinary care."),
            new("Three boats dyed blue","The dye house owns three boats it can no longer tell apart. Only one holds the blue that leaves a clean margin on a workman's shirt. Lume asks the crew to identify it by its wake.","Locate the color steward’s consignment and return the original dye vats.","The Indigo Pilot","The quay is blue to the elbow for three days. Lume calls it an excellent popular exhibition."),
            new("The rope below the rope","An older rope bridge hangs below Paz's crossing. It is used by people who can work at a height but prefer to walk home close to the sea. Neither bridge is safe until the anchor room is open.","Reach the shared anchor chambers and secure both crossings.","The Standing Knot","On the way home people choose the high rope, the low rope and occasionally the ferry. Paz is happy to count them on the other side."),
            new("The tablecloth rebellion","A magistrate has licensed every sail in the strait as a sail, including the cook's tablecloth. Jo is delighted to learn that the cloth now qualifies as a seaworthy vessel.","Capture the licensing fleet and escort the improvised kitchen boats into port.","Commodore Hem","The first meal served afloat is soup. It requires better seamanship than anyone had expected.")
        ],[
            new("The unlabeled hospital","The registry has impounded a ward ship because its number fell off. Reva can identify the ward by the rhythm of the four long taps, but the impounder's ships have begun tapping it back.","Find the true ward among the false signals and take the beds into shelter.","The Copper Auditor","A patient writes her name on the bow in letters larger than any number. The crew lets the paint dry around her fingers."),
            new("A bridge with two ears","Ume can hear a ship on either side of the bridge. A family in the foundation rooms can hear neither. An old sound gallery runs along the arch all the way to their door.","Restore the lower listening rooms and take a signal from one bank to the other.","The Stone Listener","The first message through the gallery asks how the baby slept. Both banks hear the answer at once."),
            new("The voices in transit","A buyer has packed the voice archive into freight shells. Tern says the collectors paid for the shells and have stolen everything inside them.","Locate the voice cargo and give the shells back to the households that filled them.","Captain Undertone","One recording contains three minutes of a man trying to remember what he meant to say. His daughter asks to hear all three."),
            new("The day in the cellar","Oli keeps lost calendar days underneath the meeting hall. Someone has been borrowing them to add a day to the patients' visiting hours. The small thieves have got themselves locked below.","Find the missing visitors and open the lower calendar rooms.","The Weekkeeper","Oli lets the children keep the extra afternoon. He puts one ordinary Monday back on the shelf for emergencies."),
            new("The ward beneath the ward","Pip remembers the hospital's old overflow rooms. Every door was made low enough for a child to answer from bed. Oren has spent years wondering who stayed after the ship moved.","Open the lower wards and bring the remaining patients’ wishes to the hospital fleet.","The Last Registrar","Two former patients have been running the overflow as a free clinic. Oren asks for a job and is given the washing up.")
        ],[
            new("The price of a reflection","Ada has found the ship that collects the fare for a reflection. It sails with several decoys, all paid for by charging their own shadows for passage.","Mark the real toll ship and return the duplicate fares to the families.","Captain Obverse","One halfpenny goes back to its owner after twenty years. He calls it the least profitable long-term investment of his life."),
            new("The witness underneath","Lev discovers a speaking hole under the court chairs. A clerk used it to feed answers to witnesses for thirty years. The crawlway beneath still holds the drafts of the answers people meant to give.","Open the old speaking galleries and recover the unsent testimony.","The Velvet Usher","The first child to use the hole speaks upward without being prompted. A whole row of adults puts down its papers."),
            new("News carried without sound","Edda has arranged for a family to signal its appeal using colored shutters. A customs fleet has seized the shutters as advertising. She has the appeals copied on the hinges.","Track the signal cutters and return the appeals to public view.","The Notices Gull","Edda teaches the customs crew the signal for a good apology. It takes both hands."),
            new("The kitchen sentence","Mik finds the old prison meal lift runs down to an unlisted wing. Its occupants do their own cooking and have been sending better food upstairs for years.","Explore the lower meal galleries and open the cooks’ way out.","The Iron Apron","The old cooks open a stall outside the gate. People begin arriving at the prison a little before noon on purpose."),
            new("A hearing on the water","The court has moved the public bench aboard a sealed squadron so nobody ashore can attend. Pip has read the rules twice. They say nothing about people getting there by boat.","Board the moving court and open its gangway to the witness fleet.","The Floating Bailiff","Pip calls the meeting to order with an oar. Nell records the location as Everywhere Afloat.")
        ],[
            new("The minute boats","Hester finds a fleet arriving a minute before its own departure stamp. Every minute taken from the fleet is missing from somebody’s dinner break.","Read the private time signals, take the clock ships and return the minutes.","The Spare Hand","Six harbor cooks sit down together for precisely as long as the soup takes."),
            new("The ballast nursery","Tern's scale has detected a hollow chamber under the ballast banks. Some of the missing weight of the fleet is down there, alive and still drawing wages in lead.","Go below the ballast floors and reunite the missing hands with their berths.","The Lead Sleeve","Tern weighs the boat again. Under Ships Company he writes Enough People and puts the weights away."),
            new("The ship with someone else’s view","A salvage captain has fitted Miri's windows to the cabin of a prize ship. Its owner can see eight different homes without leaving his bed. The people in the homes are starting to see him back.","Identify the ship through its traveling windows and return the panes.","Captain Fanlight","One family asks to keep the view of the sea. Miri trades them her own kitchen window and puts a curtain up."),
            new("No address below","The registry wants to number the doors in Elo's underground street. Nobody below wants a number, but the children need a way to find the high door in a flood.","Open a public flood passage through the unnamed street without marking the private doors.","The Brass Knocker","Every child can find the high door by counting the handrails. Elo paints all the street doors a different shade of nobody else's business."),
            new("The hand beneath the needle","A maintenance stair runs under Gauge’s chart engine. The crews that oiled its axle wrote the names of their own harbors where the compass could never point.","Reach the underside of the compass and raise the engineers' page to daylight.","The Hidden Pivot","Gauge reads the first harbor name in her own apprentice handwriting. She pauses over it and hands the page to Pip.")
        ]
    ];
}
